  "text": "# The Sum of the First n Cubes: A Complete Derivation\n\n## Part 1: Derivation from First Principles\n\nWe seek a closed form for the sum of the first $n$ cubes:\n\n$$S_n = \\sum_{k=1}^{n} k^3 = 1^3 + 2^3 + 3^3 + \\cdots + n^3$$\n\n### The Key Insight: A Telescoping Argument\n\nThe most elegant derivation from first principles uses a **telescoping sum** built from the difference of fourth powers. The strategy is:\n\n1. Express $k^3$ as a difference of consecutive fourth powers (up to a constant factor).\n2. Sum over all $k$ from 1 to $n$.\n3. Watch the middle terms cancel, leaving only boundary terms.\n\n### Step 1: Expand the Difference of Fourth Powers\n\nConsider the difference between consecutive fourth powers",
